0,Itneg people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Itneg_people,"The Itneg people also known as "" Tinguian "" or "" Tingguian "" are an Austronesian ethnic group indigenous to the Philippines. They are part of the broader Cordilleran or Igorot group, despite the Itnegs themselves not identifying as such.","Itneg, Inlaud",Austronesian
1,Austronesian peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austronesian_peoples,"The Austronesian peoples, sometimes referred to as Austronesian-speaking peoples, [45] are a large collection of peoples who speak Austronesian languages, having settled in Taiwan, maritime Southeast Asia, parts of mainland Southeast Asia, Micronesia, coastal New Guinea, Island Melanesia, Polynesia, and Madagascar. [46][47] They also include indigenous ethnic minorities in Vietnam, Cambodia ...","Itneg, Inlaud",Austronesian
2,"Itneg, Inlaud Language (ITI) - L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/iti/,"Inlaud Itneg is an endangered indigenous language of the Philippines. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Itneg, Inlaud",Austronesian
