4,Itneg Language of the Philippines - SINAUNANGPANAHON,https://sinaunangpanahon.com/itneg-language-of-the-philippines/,"The Itneg Language (or Tingguian Language) is an Austronesian Language spoken primarily by the Tingguian People in Abra Province, Philippines. It belongs to the Northern Luzon Languages group and has several distinct dialects.","Itneg, Inlaud",Austronesian
5,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLnOSH5j1sQh9pFS_rqvm3r2JtCD8AGOa-,"Austronesian culture includes more than 1200 ethnic groups, across South Asia, Southeast Asia, Taiwan, the Philippines, parts of China, as well as the Pacific as far afield as the Maori in New ...","Itneg, Inlaud",Austronesian
6,Itneg Inlaud | Philippine Indigenous Languages Lecture Series,https://linguistics.upd.edu.ph/events/itneg-inlaud-philippine-indigenous-languages-lecture-series/,"ABSTRACT: Serial verb construction (SVC) is a feature documented in many language groups in the world including Austronesian languages in the Pacific, Indonesia, and the Philippines. Itneg Inlaud [iti], a Meso-Cordilleran language spoken in Northern Luzon, Philippines, also exhibits this feature.","Itneg, Inlaud",Austronesian
7,Austronesian Languages (Cognation & Comparing) | Insalay is traditional ...,https://www.facebook.com/groups/austronesian.languages/posts/1960395811550091/,"The Inlaud people speak a dialect of the **Itneg language**, with some influences from Ilocano, which is widely spoken in the region. Jacqueline Hampton and 6 others 7 reactions Highlanderz Vlog 15w · Public Palakis or Pinanyuan Dance of Abra Performers: Gawis Culture and Arts Ensemble/CompanyDISCLAIMER: This dance represents Abra traditions,","Itneg, Inlaud",Austronesian
8,Itneg Culture and Heritage in Abra,https://www.scribd.com/document/860700640/Itneg,"The Itneg, an indigenous Austronesian group in the Philippines, primarily reside in the Cordillera region and are divided into nine subgroups. They maintain rich cultural practices, including agriculture, weaving, and spiritual rituals, while facing challenges such as cultural assimilation, language decline, and economic pressures. Efforts to preserve their heritage include educational ...","Itneg, Inlaud",Austronesian
9,Abra Heritage | PDF | Agriculture | Wedding,https://www.scribd.com/document/818668496/Abra-Heritage,"The document provides an overview of the historical and socio-cultural features of the Tingguians, also known as Itneg, in Abra, highlighting their geographical settlements, ethnolinguistic groups, and cultural practices. It details the division of Tingguians into lowland and upland groups, their ancestral origins, and the significance of their music and dances in rituals. Additionally, it ...","Itneg, Inlaud",Austronesian
